# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# In QEMU: fed from /dev/zero, the
# entropy PD's repetition count test fails on its first bytes; it hands out no
# seed, reports which test failed and faults on purpose; the supervisor stops
# it, reports it and resets the board; the system starts again and fails the
# same way. QEMU reboots rather than exiting (no -no-reboot): qemu-test fails
# a run in which QEMU exits, and the second boot shows the reset took.
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children entropy (0) and seed_consumer (1)
NOWAYOS: entropy: starting
NOWAYOS: entropy: virtio-rng on transport 8, claimed to give 8 bits a byte
NOWAYOS: entropy: health test failed: the repetition count test: no more seeds
NOWAYOS: supervisor: entropy stopped: a fault the supervisor does not decode
NOWAYOS: supervisor: resetting the board
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children entropy (0) and seed_consumer (1)
NOWAYOS: entropy: health test failed: the repetition count test: no more seeds
NOWAYOS: supervisor: entropy stopped: a fault the supervisor does not decode

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match),
# including in the second after the last line above: any sign of a seed taken
# from the stuck source - the start-up tests passed, a ring filled, a consumer
# seeded or drawing - a fault the monitor sees, a kernel error, the reset
# returning or a PD not stopped.
!start-up tests passed
!full:
!seeded
!seed-consumer: drew
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!the reset returned
!NOT stopped
!gave up
